   "design": "Base data and aerial photographs come from national web services by a saved script per map area, instead of mail requests and downloads one area at a time. Scanned archives are searched in full text, and the cartographer still reads the originals because text recognition errs. Digital survey files import into the GIS, and older notes are still typed. The metadata catalogue fills at import, instead of a separate spreadsheet. Checking sources, visits, clarifying and loading checks stay with the cartographer.",
